  "raw": {
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499671/visiting-assistant-extension-educator-in-land-use": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Extension Educator in Land Use",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Extension Educator in Land Use Apply now Search #: 499671 Work type: Full-time Location: Middlesex County Extension Ctr Categories: Faculty Extension Educator INTRODUCTION We seek an individual whose professional skills and abilities can provide statewide outreach and training to land use commissioners and others on issues related to land use planning and decision making. This position (Visiting Assistant Extension Educator in Land Use) will lead the award-winning Land Use Academy in the Center for Land Use Education and Research , advance the Center’s mission of supporting communities in balancing growth and natural resource protection, and have the opportunity to contribute to efforts to connect undergraduates with community extension work. The ideal candidate will have professional, municipal-level experience in land use planning, an understanding of community resilience in extreme weather events, and experience in outreach or teaching on these topics. This non-tenure track faculty level position reports to the Head of the Department of Extension, College of Agriculture and Natural Resources. The Department of Extension in the College of Agriculture, Health and Natural Resources works collaboratively with partners in all 169 municipalities across Connecticut, throughout the northeast region and beyond. It is a non-tenuring unit with 35 faculty, 30 program and administrative staff. Additional grant-specific program personnel assist to solve problems and enhance the wellbeing of our state citizens where they live, work, and learn. Work carried out by the department constitutes much of the UConn Extension System. Faculty and staff conduct activities through eight county/community-based offices and may be co-located with additional community/agency based working partners when applicable. The University serves as a beacon of academic and research excellence as well as a center for innovation and social service to communities. The University and CAHNR prioritize scholarship in areas that impact quality of life, including human, animal, plant and environmental health and sustainability. We encourage and provide support for cross-disciplinary, collaborative scholarship across the College, University, nation, and globe. UConn is committed to Life Transforming Education for students and Extension audiences. UConn is recognized as one of the most sustainable and environmentally friendly campuses by the Sierra Club. Through research, teaching, service, and Extension, UConn embraces diversity and inclusion, and cultivates leadership, integrity, and engaged citizenship in its students, faculty, staff, and alumni. Founded in 1881, UConn is a Land Grant and Sea Grant institution and member of the Space Grant Consortium. It is the state’s flagship institution of higher education and includes a main campus in Storrs, CT, four regional campuses throughout the state, and 13 Schools and Colleges, including a Law School in Hartford and Medical and Dental Schools at the UConn Health campus in Farmington. The University has approximately 10,000 faculty and staff and 32,000 students, including nearly 24,000 undergraduates and over 8,000 graduate and professional students. UConn is a Carnegie Foundation R1 (highest research activity) institution and is ranked among the top 25 public universities in the nation. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES The successful incumbent will: Develop and implement Extension programs to provide information, education, and technical assistance to community land use decision makers on a wide range of planning topics, including comprehensive planning, open space planning, conducting community resource inventories, economic development, affordable housing, resilience, and roles and responsibilities of land use commissioners. This work will include, but is not limited to: developing Extension education programs, tools and materials for land use decision makers and other audiences, including workshops (formal and informal), publications, and web information; evaluation of programs; and writing of grant proposals and project reports; Lead the Land Use Academy (LUA), a UConn CLEAR outreach program that focuses on basic and advanced training for land use commissioners; Work with the CT State Office of Policy and Management (OPM), the CT Chapter of the American Planning Association, CT Bar Association, and related agencies to identify and meet the needs of land use commissioners in complying with new mandated land use training requirements; Assist with efforts to connect undergraduate students with outreach to municipalities on land use and resilience issues; Assist in developing and delivering outreach programs focused on natural resource protection, farmland protection and access, housing availability and other pressing issues; Support and enhance access to online training courses, including required training by CT DEEP; and, Integrate the LUA training program with other CLEAR research and outreach programs, with the Connecticut Sea Grant program, and with existing and new partner organizations involved with training local officials. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Master’s Degree in land use planning, natural resources, environmental management, or related discipline; Two years’ professional experience in a field related to land use planning, preferably as a town, regional or consulting planner; Demonstrated experience with municipal land use issues, roles, and responsibilities; Demonstrated experience with the connection between land use activities and sustainability; Demonstrated communication skills, including public speaking and writing of educational materials; Interpersonal skills; Demonstrated experience working as a member of a diverse project team, as well as experience working independently; Experience with standard office word processing, spreadsheet and internet browsing software. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience working directly with local land use commissioners or other officials on community planning issues, including economic development, housing, resiliency, and natural resource protection; Experience in developing and delivering effective educational materials, workshops and presentations; AICP certified planner; Experience with land use planning and policy in Connecticut; Demonstrated experience in resiliency planning at the local level; Demonstrated successful experience in grant writing; Experience as funded project director/manager; Experience in teaching; Experience with Geographic Information Systems/geospatial technologies; Experience with Cooperative Extension or similar non-advocacy, research-based, educational programming; Experience with developing online training materials and courses. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a visiting full-time, 11-month, non-tenure track position with an anticipated start date of August 22, 2026. This is currently a grant-funded position with annual review. The successful candidate will work primarily at the University of Connecticut’s Middlesex County extension office located in Haddam, CT, with occasional travel to the Storrs Campus, other extension centers, and elsewhere in the state. The selected incumbent will be required to travel to meeting sites, including some out-of-state travel, and work a flexible schedule, which may include occasional evenings and weekends, to reach target audiences. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499671 and submit the following application materials: A cover letter , Curriculum vitae , Name and Contact information for 3 professional reference s. At the University of Connecticut, our commitment to excellence is complemented by our commitment to building a culturally diverse community. Evaluation of applicants will begin immediately and the position will remain open until filled. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499870/business-advisor-parttime-educational-program-administrator-ct-small-business-development-center": {
      "title": "Business Advisor, Part-Time (Educational Program Administrator), CT Small Business Development Center",
      "description": "Business Advisor, Part-Time (Educational Program Administrator), CT Small Business Development Center Apply now Search #: 499870 Work type: Part-time Location: Other - please see posting for additional information Categories: Administrative Services JOB SUMMARY The Connecticut Small Business Development Center (CTSBDC) in the School of Business is seeking a part-time (70%) Business Advisor (Educational Program Administrator). The incumbent will report to the CTSBDC Associate State Director and will advise and counsel individuals seeking to start a business, covering management, finance, marketing, and licensing and registration topics, and providing an overview of tax obligations and other topics. The incumbent will provide information on federal, state, and local registration requirements. This position acts as a consultant, advocate and liaison for all CTSBDC services and resources, collaborating with state agencies on behalf of entrepreneurs and small business owners. The position will be based at the CTSBDC Lead Office in East Hartford, CT. Dependable transportation is required, as well as a willingness and ability to work flexible hours and travel in-state and out-of-state as needed to support program activities. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Include but are not limited to: Providing technical and management assistance to the small business community via on-site visits, online platforms, email and phone. Providing in-depth counseling and recommending course of action to owners of small businesses or to those about to start a business, in key areas such as business models and plans, startup financing, presentation of financial material, evaluation of current financial condition, industry specific federal and state regulations, and marketing products/services; addressing topics including, but not limited to market research, marketing strategies, and customer acquisition; international trade import/export; general understanding of organizational issues related to business structure; operations; accounting/financial analysis; federal, state and local resources for startup and young businesses; and veterans’, women’s, and minority business issues. Assisting clients in developing and recording their business concepts and using industry tools such as the Business Model Canvas and business plan outlines. Maintaining and enhancing the SBDC program’s ability and capacity to offer reasoned, logical advice and guidance on all matters of starting, building, and sustaining a business. Enhancing and delivering quality programs to the CTSBDC client base and CTSBDC colleagues, including planning, coordinating, and evaluating the success of advising, learning, and training programs. Keeping current on and informing clients about changes or current developments in regulations, laws, or conditions that may affect their business. Conducting and/or coordinating on-site administration of community outreach, client development, informational, and training programs, and making all arrangements necessary to deliver these programs. Working toward the goal that each client request receives a response within forty-eight hours during the business week, and offering an initial consultation with a client within two weeks of the client assignment. Performing necessary administrative duties such as correspondence, progress and summary reports, and the collection of data as required and utilized by the funding agency. Annually identifying personal professional development initiatives in accordance with guidelines determined in conjunction with supervisors and striving to complete an approved professional development plan within the given program year. Participating in ASBDC annual conference and NEPD annual event as determined in conjunction with the Director or Associate Director. Building and maintaining effective working relationships with public agencies, service organizations, and the private sector in order to better assist clients and to keep informed of general business conditions and changes in regulations/laws affecting small business. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in business, counseling, social work, or related field. At least five years of experience in an entrepreneurial, business management, financial, counseling or business education environment, project management, or experience with SBDC program methodology. One year of experience must be serving as an advanced team member. Demonstrated ability to assess the unique needs of each business and relay that information clearly and succinctly. Demonstrated ability to advise, counsel, and mentor individuals from diverse backgrounds, cultures, and financial situations. Proven ability to plan, conduct and implement client development, recruitment and training programs. Demonstrated experience taking initiative, working independently and accurately, exercising sound judgment when making decisions, and meeting deadlines. Demonstrated proficiency with mobile device technology including smartphones and tablets. Demonstrated excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills and the ability to build and maintain collaborative relationships with faculty, staff, students, administrators, external agencies/groups and the public. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree in business, counseling, social work, or related field Ability to conduct advising and training sessions in Spanish. Spanish proficiency. Familiarity with web-based client tracking systems, CRMs. Experience in counseling or advising small business owners and entrepreneurs. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS The prorated salary range for this position is $56,000 to $57,680 (full-time salary range is $80,000 to $82,400). An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves header at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA) and look for information specifically identified for UCPEA, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a part-time, 12-month, annually renewable position. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499870 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on October 20, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 06 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 20 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499856/research-associate-rural-health": {
      "title": "Research Associate (Rural Health)",
      "description": "Research Associate (Rural Health) Apply now Search #: 499856 Work type: Full-time Location: Other - please see posting for additional information Categories: Research JOB SUMMARY The Innovations Institute at the University of Connecticut School of Social Work seeks a Research Associate 1 to support the evaluation of the Connecticut Rural Health Transformation Program (CT RHTP), a five-year, statewide initiative funded by the Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) and administered by the Connecticut Department of Social Services. The evaluation team is responsible for developing and implementing an overarching framework to measure implementation, outcomes, and sustainability across 30 projects spanning four initiative areas: Population Health, Workforce, Data and Technology, and Care Transformation and Stability. Positions with the Innovations Institute are fully remote, with expected travel to UConn's Hartford Campus twice annually. The Research Associate 1 will work with the project Principal Investigator and Co-Directors to contribute methodological and analytic expertise across the CT RHTP evaluation and will report to the Principal Investigator. This includes assisting with facilitating, and when appropriate, leading the design of research and evaluation plans, conducting quantitative and mixed-methods analyses, translating findings into products for diverse audiences, and providing technical assistance to project teams, state agencies, and community partners. The Research Associate 1 will also contribute to cross-project learning and continuous quality improvement, co-author academic and public-facing products, and help ensure that data security, privacy, and compliance requirements are met across all participating entities. This position also requires project management, including communicating with project staff and external partners, facilitating meetings, and coordinating and aligning efforts across projects and initiatives. This position is well suited to a doctoral-level researcher with training and experience in health services research, program evaluation, and implementation science, and a strong interest in improving healthcare access and outcomes in rural communities. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Assist with, facilitate, and co-lead the design and development of research and evaluation plans, including study design, sampling, measurement, data collection procedures, and analytic strategy across assigned projects. Work directly with stakeholders and project teams to identify research and evaluation needs and translate them into rigorous, feasible study designs that support continuous quality improvement (CQI) and evaluation goals. Assist with, facilitate, and co-lead quantitative and mixed-methods analytic plans, applying appropriate statistical methods and interpreting findings to generate actionable insights. Manage complex data sets and primary data using statistical software (e.g., Excel, SPSS, SAS, R, STATA), and establish processes to ensure data quality, accuracy, and analysis readiness. Conduct literature reviews and synthesize evidence to inform study design, contextualize findings, and support evidence-based recommendations. Provide technical assistance to service providers and public agencies in developing data collection procedures, building instruments, reviewing data, and resolving data quality issues. Develop data visualizations tailored to internal and external stakeholders that clearly communicate complex findings. Facilitate the preparation and management of Data Use Agreements (DUAs), IRB submissions, and related compliance documentation. Independently write and co-author products, including academic manuscripts, public-facing one-pagers, and technical reports for decision-makers. Supervise, mentor, and provide guidance to graduate students and other research staff on data collection, analysis, storage, and reporting, and review their work for quality and accuracy. Serve as a subject-matter expert in program evaluation, implementation science, and quantitative data analysis for internal and external partners. Assist with the Rural Health Evaluation Advisory Board and the evaluators' Community of Practice (CoP). Coordinate and facilitate internal and external communications and meetings. Co-author manuscripts in peer-reviewed journals and present findings at academic and professional conferences. Contribute to the development and writing of federal, state, and private grant proposals. Contribute to and manage work plans, ensuring milestones and reporting deadlines are met. Perform other duties as needed. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Master's degree in Social Sciences, Social Work, Education, Public Policy, Public Health, Health Science, Statistics, Economics, or another field of study related to research. Demonstrated ability to develop and maintain relevant subject-matter knowledge related to rural health, health services, program evaluation, and the RHTP initiative areas. Experience performing literature reviews and presenting results. Demonstrated knowledge of research study design and data collection procedures, and the ability to understand and use scientific terminology and research theory. Demonstrated knowledge of regulations governing the confidentiality of subjects and the ability to maintain the confidentiality of information obtained. Evidence of skill in statistical programming, data and statistical analysis, and interpreting findings using statistical software (e.g., SPSS, SAS, R, STATA). Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects at once, respond to tight timelines, pay close attention to detail, and operate effectively in a fast-paced environment. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. in Social Sciences, Social Work, Education, Public Policy, Public Health, Health Science, Statistics, Economics, or another field of study related to research. Experience developing and maintaining effective working relationships with partners, including funders, internal colleagues, and other stakeholders, and partnering with diverse stakeholders to develop research agendas related to outcomes, feedback, and evaluations. Demonstrated skill in using measurable and verifiable information for making decisions and judgments. Experience supervising or mentoring graduate students, trainees, or junior research staff in a research or evaluation setting. Demonstrated knowledge of implementation science, rapid-cycle evaluation, and data visualization. Experience supervising other analysts, including drafting evaluation plans. Demonstrated ability to convey complex information clearly, in writing and orally, so that it is easily understood by stakeholders and organizations. Stated willingness to learn and effectively use new technology, maintaining productivity and using strategies to increase knowledge base. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, end-dated position with the possibility of renewal subject to performance and available funding. Positions with the Innovations Institute are fully remote and expected to travel to UConn's Hartford Campus once a year at the employee's expense. Candidates who reside in Connecticut to engage in in-person project activities are preferred. The salary range for this position is $85,000 to $111,000, commensurate with education and experience. The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits, including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment. For additional information regarding benefits, please visit UConn Health Benefits and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves and Engagement & Learning headers. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the American Association of University Professors (AAUP). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499856 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on December 1, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 02 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Dec 01 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499791/continuous-quality-improvement-manager-research-scientist": {
      "title": "Continuous Quality Improvement Manager (Research Scientist)",
      "description": "Continuous Quality Improvement Manager (Research Scientist) Apply now Search #: 499791 Work type: Full-time Location: Other - please see posting for additional information Categories: Research JOB SUMMARY Innovations Institute is seeking applicants for the Continuous Quality Improvement Manager (Research Scientist). The successful candidate will direct continuous quality improvement (CQI) efforts across Innovations’ disseminated practice models, including Wraparound, Mobile Response and Stabilization Services (MRSS), FOCUS, and PEARLS. The contribution will be measured in terms of CQI deliverables completed across contracted states and sites. Successful candidates will be expected to broaden participation among members of underrepresented groups; demonstrate, through research and/or community engagement, a commitment to and support for diversity in the learning experience; and integrate multicultural experiences into CQI tools, reports, and conversations. Positions with Innovations Institute are fully remote with expected travel to UConn’s Hartford Campus twice annually at the employee's expense. Candidates must have a willingness to learn how to effectively use new technology. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Under the direction of the Division's leadership, lead the strategic planning, implementation, and evaluation of continuous quality improvement (CQI) systems across the division’s disseminated practice models, including Wraparound, MRSS, FOCUS, and PEARLS. Support the design, refinement, and dissemination of fidelity and quality assurance tools in collaboration with internal staff and contracted states and sites. Establish and oversee PDCA (Plan-Do-Check-Act) cycles with state and contract partners to translate CQI data into practice-, organization-, and system-level improvements. Ensure CQI deliverables align with contract scopes of work and University policies and expectations. Foster close working relationships with internal coaches and contracted states and sites to identify implementation challenges and CQI needs. Supervise assigned CQI and data staff, providing direction, performance oversight, and professional development. Lead discussions and initiatives about CQI infrastructure, new programs, symposia, workshops, and other dissemination events. Lead the development and dissemination of white papers, briefs, peer-reviewed journal articles, and conference posters showcasing CQI findings and outcomes. Clearly communicate CQI capabilities, tools, and findings to state leaders and contract partners. Coordinate deliverable timelines and CQI reporting in collaboration with senior leadership, division director, and support staff. Prepare accurate and succinct CQI reports for state and contract partners, ensuring alignment with deliverable requirements and expectations. Ensure compliance with contract, funder, and regulatory requirements governing CQI activities. Facilitate collaboration between division program teams and state CQI and data leads. Direct CQI and data management processes supporting the division’s internal operations, including internal reporting, workflow improvement, and data systems. Serve as subject matter expert for state leaders, sites, faculty, staff, and division partners on matters relating to CQI policies, procedures, and services. Responsible for Institutional Review Board (IRB) submissions where warranted. Work on related special projects as directed by leadership. Perform related duties as required. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Earned Ph.D. in social work, public health, psychology, public policy/administration, program evaluation, health services research, applied methodology, or a related field. Equivalent foreign degrees are acceptable. Demonstrated experience leading continuous quality improvement (CQI), fidelity measurement, or systems evaluation efforts in behavioral health or human services settings. Experience partnering with diverse stakeholders to develop CQI agendas related to outcomes, feedback, and evaluations. Experience with creating data visualizations and communicating data-based findings with diverse audiences. Evidence of strong organizational skills, including the ability to manage multiple projects at once, respond to tight timelines, pay attention to detail, and operate effectively in a fast-paced environment. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Demonstrated technical proficiency in CQI data systems, dashboards, and reporting and statistical software (e.g., WrapSTAT, Power BI, SPSS, R, SAS, or Stata), and the ability to learn and troubleshoot new technologies. Experience working with children and their caregivers within behavioral health or child-serving systems. Experience with PDCA methodology and/or implementation tool development and refinement. Experience developing and maintaining effective working relationships with partners, including funders, internal colleagues, and other stakeholders. Demonstrated skill in using measurable and verifiable information for making decisions and judgments. Demonstrated knowledge of implementation science. Experience merging, cleaning, and analyzing skill development tool databases. Demonstrated ability to convey complex information in writing and orally so that it is easily understood by stakeholders and organizations. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $100,000 to $145,000. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves and Engagement & Learning headers at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the American Association of University Professors (AAUP) bargaining unit and look for information specifically identified as AAUP, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, 11-month, non-tenure-track position with an anticipated start date of November 6, 2026. Positions with Innovations Institute are fully remote with expected travel to UConn’s Hartford Campus twice annually at the employee's expense. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499791 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting will remain open until filled. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Aug 25 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499874/educational-program-coordinator-p3": {
      "title": "Educational Program Coordinator P3",
      "description": "Educational Program Coordinator P3 Apply now Search #: 499874 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Administrative Services JOB SUMMARY The Connecticut Training and Technical Assistance Center seeks applications for the position of Educational Program Coordinator (P3). Under the direction of the Executive Director, the position provides programmatic support to the Center, including event and project coordination. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Coordinates with subject matter experts to provide curriculum development support for educational programs offered by the CT Training & Technical Assistance Center at the University of Connecticut. Conducts needs assessments for future training needs, compiles and presents data to center leadership, making suggestions for future sessions. Coordinates with instructors to schedule the Center’s training sessions throughout Connecticut. Serves as the facilitator for onsite workshops. Coordinates with Center staff to develop promotional outreach to bring awareness to specific training opportunities for targeted audiences. Develops virtual learning opportunities for municipal, state, and private sector audiences. Coordinates outreach and events to support workforce development efforts. Serve as a resource to individuals and groups on matters relating to program activities. Other duties and projects as assigned. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree. At least four years of experience with the development of curriculum and/or learning resources for adult learners. Demonstrated ability to work independently and regularly exercise judgment regarding program support details and procedures. Demonstrated organizational skills, including the ability to prioritize, multitask, and follow through. Technical skills including demonstrated proficiency in Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and other Office 365 applications. Demonstrated verbal, written, and interpersonal communication skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience with instructional design and development of virtual learning programs. Experience with project and event management. Experience with supporting non-profit or grant-funded organizations. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $65,000 to $70,000. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves header at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA) and look for information specifically identified for UCPEA, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, end-dated position with the possibility of renewal subject to performance and funding. The chosen candidate must have the ability to travel to multiple work locations within Connecticut and the region as well as the ability to occasionally work extended hours. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499874 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on October 23, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 09 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 23 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499851/assistant-director-student-services-program-assistant-2-asian-american-cultural-center": {
      "title": "Assistant Director (Student Services Program Assistant 2), Asian American Cultural Center",
      "description": "Assistant Director (Student Services Program Assistant 2), Asian American Cultural Center Apply now Search #: 499851 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Student Programs and Services OPEN TO CURRENT UCONN EMPLOYEES ONLY JOB SUMMARY Reporting to the Director of the Asian American Cultural Center (AsACC), the Assistant Director is responsible for the internal operation of the Center, assists in program development and execution, provides assistance to promote Asian/Asian American student success and helps in fostering partnerships across campus and beyond. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Responsible for the hiring, supervision, training, work schedules, and evaluation of the student staff and practicum students. Develop, advise, and inform the staff and users of the Center regarding policies, procedures, personnel issues, and other matters pertaining to effective and efficient operations of the AsACC; update and maintain operation manuals for the AsACC. Assist in the planning, coordinating, and marketing of all programs for the AsACC. Collaborate and be the Center lead in developing new programs and initiatives with other cultural centers and program offices within the Office for Student Life & Enrollment and other University offices/department. Provide support, advocacy, and/or resource/referral information, as needed to students, staff, and faculty. Coordinate the annual Senior Banquet and the multiple scholarship awards process. Serve as the AsACC liaison to the Asian American Alumni Association and assist in the development of joint programming to foster continued connection among students and alumni. Research grants and other funding opportunities for the AsACC. Represent the AsACC at meetings with other University offices or external groups as needed. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS UConn employee on regular payroll. Bachelor’s degree and a minimum of 2 years of related professional experience in an Asian American/multicultural center or non-profit/community setting or similar field of work. Comprehensive knowledge of the Asian/Asian American community and ability to apply theories of identity and student development to carry out the mission of the Asian American Cultural Center. Demonstrated ability to deal effectively with the public, students, faculty, staff, alumni, and external agencies. Proven ability to evaluate, problem-solve, and troubleshoot to resolve difficult situations. Experience with supervision and evaluation of student staff. Demonstrated effective organizational, operational, and management skills. Excellent oral and written communication skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree in Student Affairs, counseling, or a related specialty area. More than 2 years of related professional experience in an Asian American/multicultural center or non-profit/community setting or similar field of work. Training in diversity education, social justice, cultural competency, or other related fields. Knowledge of assessment evaluation related to student learning and development. Experience working with student organizations. COMPENSATION & BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $55,000 to $70,126. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves header at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA) and look for information specifically identified for UCPEA, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS This position is a full-time, 12-month position and requires occasional night and weekend hours. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499851 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on October 23, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 09 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 23 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
