    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499118/supplier-engagement-program-manager": {
      "title": "Supplier Engagement Program Manager",
      "description": "Supplier Engagement Program Manager Apply now Search #: 499118 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Administrative Services JOB SUMMARY The University’s Procurement team is seeking a mission-driven Supplier Engagement Program Manager who is committed to expanding opportunities for Connecticut suppliers and building meaningful connections between the University and the businesses that serve Connecticut. The successful candidate will play a key role in strengthening UConn’s supplier engagement strategy, increasing participation among Connecticut-based businesses, and helping suppliers navigate opportunities with UConn. This position manages and supervises all administrative services for the University Supplier Engagement Program (USEP) and is accountable for performing and managing the most complex tasks within the USEP. Responsibilities include but are not limited to leading the development and implementation of the University and UConn Heath’s (UCH) vendor engagement strategy and supervising activities, reports, and processes of a team serving the University’s main campus in Storrs, all regional campuses, and UConn Health in Farmington. This position is located at the main campus in Storrs, CT but requires a flexible schedule and regular in-state travel to conduct training, outreach and attend meetings and events. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBIBLITIES Responsible for the effectiveness of all University and UCH supplier engagement programs. Directs the day-to-day operation and administration of USEP, and assists in the planning, direction, coordination and expansion of USEP. Works collaboratively with various offices within the University and UCH and serves as an advisor to university administrators, staff, business leaders and/or other constituents regarding policies, procedures, statutory requirements and reporting responsibilities specific to USEP. Serves as USEP liaison to Department of Administrative Services and the Commission on Human Rights with regard to developing and executing complex supplier diversity strategies to increase participation and meet statutory goals. Performs office management duties for USEP; prepares comprehensive analyses, reports and recommendations for administrative decision-making; and supervises, trains and evaluates assigned personnel. Plans, organizes and administers workshops and training programs, in accordance with program goals. Represents the University and UCH in key supplier engagement related organizations, committees and conferences. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree, preferably in Business or related field and a minimum of five (5) years professional experience in procurement of materials/commodities in a comparable environment OR an Associate’s degree in a closely related field and seven (7) or more years of related professional experience in a comparable environment, OR an equivalency of education and relevant experience which includes at least nine (9) years’ professional experience in procurement of materials/commodities in a comparable environment. Experience in supplier relationship management, including oversight of performance and compliance. Strong leadership, supervisory, organizational, project management, and planning skills with the ability to meet deadlines and facilitate solutions in a fast-paced environment. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Knowledge of and experience in negotiating, administering and supervising procurement and business-related activities. General knowledge of supplier engagement principles, laws, regulations and applicable federal and state procurement statutes and policies. Ability to develop and implement supplier engagement and other supplier related strategies and activities. Ability to identify and resolve complex issues efficiently, effectively and independently. Strong interpersonal and persuasiveness skills and the ability to work effectively with all levels of employees and management. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, permanent position located at the Storrs campus. The department is currently working under a hybrid model requiring staff to be on the Storrs campus two (2) days per week and to work remotely three (3) days per week. The hybrid work schedule may change subject to authorization and University policy. The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits , including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment. The annual salary will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s background and experience. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT This position requires regular travel. Successful candidate must have dependable transportation and must be willing and able to work occasional evenings and weekends. Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499118 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . References will not be contacted without prior notice to the successful candidate(s). Screening will begin immediately. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on October 30, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499450/contract-specialist-1": {
      "title": "Contract Specialist 1",
      "description": "Contract Specialist 1 Apply now Search #: 499450 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Grants and Contracts JOB SUMMARY The University of Connecticut seeks to hire a Contract Specialist to support the Procurement Contracting & Compliance team with a variety of contracts in support of the needs of the campus community. Under the general direction of the University Director of Procurement Contracting & Compliance and/or the Senior Contract Specialist, this role will utilize existing policies, procedures, and statutes to draft and negotiate terms and conditions for a variety of university contracts. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES include but are not limited to: Drafts and negotiates contract language for various contracts under assigned commodities. Responsible for the administration of all contractual activities for University Procurement Contracting & Compliance, as they relate to the needs of the University community. Collaborate with internal customer departments and colleagues within Procurement, as needed, to draft clear contracts that accurately capture the negotiated business terms. Represents the department with authority to act on behalf of the University Director, when expressly authorized. Ensures proper controls over contracting procedures for sound fiscal and administrative management and compliance with state ethics codes. Responsible for preparation and legal review of contracts and agreements submitted to the Office of the General Counsel and Office of the Attorney General. Monitors and tracks contracts and related documents for compliance with State and Federal statutes, Board of Trustees policies, Office of the General Counsel/Attorney General guidelines, internal procedures formulated by the University, and contract terms and conditions. Prepares and manages reports; maintains knowledge of, and interprets, applicable State and Federal statutes and regulations, Board of Trustees policies, Office of the General Counsel/Attorney General Guidelines, and the State’s Code of Ethics; provides information, instruction and/or training, as needed or requested, in relation to university compliance with contractual matters. Inform customers and/or vendors on new and/or current procurement procedures and guidelines. Analyzes technical data, i.e., scope of work and pricing information, vendor performance, and compliance with finalizing contracts. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in business, or a related field and four years of related professional experience in a comparable environment OR an Associate’s degree in business, or a related field and six years of related professional experience in a comparable environment OR eight years of professional contracting experience in a comparable environment. General working knowledge of accepted procurement practices and the ability to negotiate contract language to address the risks related to each type of arrangement which may be used in a wide range of varying and unique commodity groups and/or services. Excellent interpersonal, oral and written communication skills. Excellent computer skills with strong technical skills to work with multiple software programs including Microsoft Office. Ability to work independently with minimal supervision under tight deadlines while managing multiple projects. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s or advanced degree in related discipline. Knowledge of contract theory, principles, laws, regulations and applicable federal and state procurement statutes, and policies. Experience developing and executing complex contracting strategies that maximize workflow efficiencies, process improvements, and operational performance. Experience with contracting in the State of Connecticut. Ability to assess organizational needs, communicate those needs to the vendor community, negotiate as needed, and evaluate contracts to determine technical compliance and resolve discrepancies. Knowledge of contract management systems automated procurement systems (e.g., Jaggaer). APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time position at the Storrs campus working Monday-Friday 8:30 a.m. – 4:30 p.m. The starting salary range for this position will be $75,000-$83,727 and final salary will be determined based on the successful candidate’s experience and training. The department is currently working under a hybrid work schedule requiring all staff to be on the Storrs campus two (2) days per week and working remotely three (3) days per week. This schedule may change subject to authorization and University policy. The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits , including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499450 to upload a resume, cover letter, and contact information for three (3) professional references. References will not be contacted without prior notice to the successful candidate(s). Screening will begin immediately. For detailed information about this position and the department, please visit our website . This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on October 16, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 16 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499824/clinical-simulation-instructor": {
      "title": "Clinical Simulation Instructor",
      "description": "Clinical Simulation Instructor Apply now Search #: 499824 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Faculty Non Tenure Track INTRODUCTION The Elisabeth DeLuca School of Nursing (SON) at the University of Connecticut invites applications to fill two full-time, 11-month, non-tenure track faculty positions at the Clinical Instructor level at our Storrs campus. Under the direction of the Director of Simulation Education, the faculty members will have the following responsibilities: supervise pre-licensure students in simulations, provide fundamentals teaching support, provide skills labs instruction, develop simulation scenarios, set up labs and simulations, post-lab cleanup, monitor simulation and lab inventory and supplies, supervise open labs for student practice, provide simulation/clinic completion and continuous improvement plans and augment support and training for the adjunct clinical faculty in the use of simulations and the Simulation Center. Founded in 1881, UConn is a Land Grant and Sea Grant institution and is a member of the Space Grant Consortium. It is the state’s flagship institution of higher education and includes a main campus in Storrs, CT, four regional campuses throughout the state, and 13 Schools and Colleges, including a Law School in Hartford, and Medical and Dental Schools at the UConn Health campus in Farmington. The University has approximately 10,000 faculty and staff and 32,000 students, including nearly 24,000 undergraduates and over 8,000 graduate and professional students. UConn is a Carnegie Foundation R1 (highest research activity) institution, among the top 25 public universities in the nation. Through research, teaching, service, and outreach, UConn embraces diversity and cultivates leadership, integrity, and engaged citizenship in its students, faculty, staff, and alumni. UConn promotes the health and well-being of citizens by enhancing the social, economic, cultural, and natural environments of the state and beyond. The university serves as a beacon of academic and research excellence as well as a center for innovation and social service to communities. UConn is a leader in many scholarly, research, and innovation areas. Today, the path forward includes exciting opportunities and notable challenges. Record numbers of undergraduate applications and support for student success have enabled the University to become extraordinarily selective. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree in Nursing. Three to five years of clinical experience in a relevant clinical area. Current Connecticut multistate compact RN license (valid as of date of hire), which must be maintained. Demonstrated communication skills and interpersonal relationship strategies. Previous clinical teaching experience. Experience evaluating student performance in clinical training settings. Experience developing effective interprofessional working relationships. Completion of required health indicators (MMR titers, TB status, Hepatitis B, and others as required by clinical agencies) and CPR certification at the time of employment. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Previous experience facilitating clinical simulations. CHSE (Certified Healthcare Simulation Educator). Previous teaching experience in an institution of higher education. Experience managing and directing “group” clinical training for students in baccalaureate nursing programs and/or accelerated nursing entry program. Experience with a wide range of educational strategies, including virtual and in-person simulation. Current experience with direct patient care in healthcare institutions and/or community settings. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS The salary for this position is $97,000. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves and Engagement & Learning headers at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the American Association of University Professors (AAUP) bargaining unit and look for information specifically identified as AAUP, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is an 11-month, non-tenure-track position subject to annual renewal based on program needs, funding, and performance. Successful candidates’ primary appointment will be at the Storrs campus, with the expectation that they may travel to assist at other School of Nursing Simulation Centers at Waterbury or Avery Point. Individuals may attain eligibility for multi-year contracts after successful completion of four (4) one-year appointments. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT The employment of successful candidates is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499824 to upload the following additional application materials. Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. A cover letter specifically addressing your credentials relative to the minimum and preferred qualifications listed above, Curriculum vitae , One-page teaching statement , One-page commitment to diversity statement (as related to broadening participation, integrating multicultural experiences in instruction and research/scholarship, and pedagogical techniques to meet the needs of diverse learning styles, etc.); Contact information for three (3) references. The evaluation of applicants will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. For more information regarding the SON please visit the School’s website . At the University of Connecticut, our commitment to excellence is complemented by our commitment to building a culturally diverse community. This position will be filled subject the budgetary approval. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 28 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499860/assistant-dean-for-finance-school-of-business-usp-3": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean for Finance, School of Business (USP 3)",
      "description": "Assistant Dean for Finance, School of Business (USP 3) Apply now Search #: 499860 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Executive JOB SUMMARY The School of Business at the University of Connecticut invites applications for the position of Assistant Dean for Finance (ADF). This senior leadership role serves as the Dean’s designee overseeing all fiscal management of the school, including human resources, information technology, facilities, and operational planning. Working collaboratively with the Associate Deans, Department Heads, and staff, the ADF ensures that these services are efficient, effective, and aligned with the mission and strategic goals of the School and the University. This position is based at the Storrs campus, but also covers School of Business operations and programs in Hartford, Stamford, and Waterbury. Occasional evenings, weekends, and in-state travel may be required. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES In consultation with the Dean, develops, evaluates, interprets, and enforces university and School policies, procedures, guidelines, and strategies. Oversees business and fiscal services, including budgeting, financial analysis, reporting, audits, and centralization of financial operations for all academic departments, centers, revenue-generating programs, and UConn Foundation partnerships within the School. Oversees School of Business relationships with university partner offices (including Provost, Budget Office, OVPR, Bursar, Purchasing, and Travel). Supervises key professional staff, including the Executive Director of Administrative Operations & Staff Development, the Executive Director of Technology Operations, and the Dean's Office fiscal team. Represents the School of Business on university committees and leadership forums when called on by the Dean. Performs other duties as required. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree in business administration, accounting, human resources, public administration, higher education administration, or related field. 7–10 years of progressively responsible experience in higher education administration or a similar complex organization. Demonstrated experience with fiscal oversight, budget development, and financial analysis. Supervisory experience managing professional staff and cross-functional teams. Demonstrated knowledge of relevant federal, state, and university regulations governing HR, finance, and business operations. Demonstrated communication, problem-solving, and policy interpretation skills. Experience with human resource management, labor relations, staff evaluations, and/or organizational development. Experience in strategic planning, organizational process improvement, or operational efficiency initiatives. Proven ability to work collaboratively with diverse stakeholders. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience with RCM Budget Models. CPA certification. At least 6 years of experience in higher education leadership, particularly in a fiscal/financial role. Proven experience using data/financial reporting to inform decisions. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, permanent, 12-month, management-exempt position with an anticipated start date in November 2026. Salary will be commensurate with experience. The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits, including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment. For additional information regarding benefits, please visit UConn Health Benefits and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves and Engagement & Learning headers. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499860 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on October 15, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 25 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 15 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499840/research-associate-or-postdoctoral-research-associate-fabris-group": {
      "title": "Research Associate or Postdoctoral Research Associate (Fabris Group)",
      "description": "Research Associate or Postdoctoral Research Associate (Fabris Group) Apply now Search #: 499840 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Postdoctoral Research Associates JOB SUMMARY The Laboratory of Dr. Dan Fabris in the Chemistry Department at the University of Connecticut, Storrs, is seeking a Research Associate/Post-Doctoral Fellow to participate in Epitranscriptomics projects aimed at investigating the functional roles of RNA post-transcriptional modifications (rPTMs) in the cell response to viral infections and other types of stresses. Highly motivated individuals holding a PhD in the Life Sciences or an M.S. degree with extensive experience are encouraged to apply. This position will be hired at either the Postdoctoral Research Associate classification or the Research Associate 1 classification, dependent upon the incumbent's experience, skills, and abilities as determined by the University. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES The Postdoctoral Research Associate or Research Associate will be responsible for the following tasks: Conduct research aimed at elucidating the dynamics of rPTMs in human cell cultures infected with HIV-1 and hepatitis C. Generate and maintain cultures in which the genes for selected rPTM writers, erasers, and readers have been effectively knocked out. Perform proper control experiments by using a variety of biochemical, spectroscopic and electrophoretic techniques. Purify viral and host RNA for advanced mass spectrometric analysis. Optimize and troubleshoot current experimental procedures. Train and lead a team of undergraduate and graduate research assistants Postdoctoral Research Associates will be responsible for these additional tasks: Participate in designing experiments and completing data analysis and interpretation. Write publications; participate in dissemination. The incumbent will be expected to use initiative in the planning and execution of the different tasks; to maintain the research productivity necessary to cultivate a presence in the scientific community; to develop a good understanding of how to best prioritize the various tasks according to the situation on the ground; to maintain the maximum possible flexibility to facilitate the solution of unforeseen problems. No direct experience is required in mass spectrometry and related techniques. If necessary, appropriate training will be provided to the new hire. The incumbent will report directly to Dr. Fabris, the laboratory’s principal investigator. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Postdoctoral Research Associate: PhD in Chemistry or a closely related field. Research Associate 1: PhD in Chemistry or a closely related field and no experience to one year of post-degree experience; or an M.A. or M.S. in Chemistry or a closely related field, and eight to ten years of post-degree experience. Experience in virology, cell biology, and gene silencing techniques. RNA biochemistry, molecular biology, and pertinent bioassays. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience with RNA sequencing (RNA-seq) techniques. Experience with next-generation sequencing (NGS) techniques. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $64,000 to $70,000. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves and Engagement & Learning headers at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. Postdoctoral Research Associate - covered by the University of Connecticut Graduate Employee & Postdoc Union bargaining unit and look for information specifically identified for Postdoctoral Research Associates, as provisions may vary by employee group. Research Associate 1 - covered by the American Association of University Professors (AAUP) bargaining unit and look for information specifically identified as AAUP, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS The salary will be commensurate with qualifications and accumulated experience. The start date for the position is anticipated for November 2026. The position is for an initial one-year appointment and is potentially renewable for a second year upon mutual agreement, funding availability, and performance. Continuation beyond two years is contingent upon future external funding applications. Postdoctoral Research Associate - Other rights and terms and conditions of your appointment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the International Union, United Automobile, Aerospace, and Agricultural Implement Workers of America (UAW), Local 6950; Research Associate 1 - Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the American Association of University Professors UConn Chapter (AAUP). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499840 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on October 26, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 24 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 26 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499225/clinical-veterinarian": {
      "title": "Clinical Veterinarian",
      "description": "Clinical Veterinarian Apply now Search #: 499225 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Executive JOB SUMMARY This full-time Clinical Veterinarian position is primarily clinical, providing veterinary care and veterinary services in support of the organization’s research mission. The Clinical Veterinarian will provide daily support to diagnose, treat, and manage clinical cases identified in the research colonies; assist with disease surveillance and prevention programs; participate in various activities to ensure compliance with regulations and guidelines; and assist the Director with administration and management of the animal care and use program. In addition, the successful candidate will provide professional service primarily in the areas of anesthesia and surgery and will oversee post-operative care of animals in support of specific research programs. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Provides direct veterinary care. Consults with and instructs investigators on the diagnosis and treatment of animals; preventive health programs; selection of animal models; selection and administration of anesthetics, analgesics, and tranquilizers; and planning and conduct of animal surgical procedures. Assists in development of training programs and participates in training of individuals who work with animals to meet regulatory and accreditation requirements. Manages preventive health programs. Advises and mentors support staff to foster their understanding of their role in animal care program processes. Collaborates with administrators, faculty, animal care staff, and the Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee (IACUC) to evaluate facilities and practices and to recommend practical and effective animal care and use procedures and maintenance systems. Provides veterinary pre-review of IACUC protocols. May serve as a voting member of the IACUC. Provide cross-campus support for UConn Health, UConn Storrs, and UConn regional campuses as needed. Perform other related duties as required. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Doctor of Veterinary Medicine (VMD/DVM) Degree from an American Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA) or Educational Commission for Foreign Veterinary Graduates (ECFVG) certificate and license to practice veterinary medicine in at least one state in the United States, with ability to obtain CT licensure upon hire. Possession of, or the ability to obtain within 12 months of hire, controlled substance licensure in the State of Connecticut. Board certification/eligibility in laboratory animal medicine or 3-5 years of relevant private practice experience (e.g., exotic and small animal practice). Demonstrated oral and written communication skills, with a proven track record of leading presentations. Demonstrated experience utilizing analytical, problem-solving, and decision-making skills with an aptitude for detailed work. Experience with computer software applications (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, etc.). PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS USDA-accredited veterinarian. Evidence of completion of advanced training in laboratory animal medicine; veterinary anesthesiology, surgery or emergency medicine; or other relevant veterinary specialties. Experience working with agricultural and/or wildlife species in research, husbandry, or field settings is a plus. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $130,000 to $150,000. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves header at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is considered management/confidential and look for information specifically identified for management/confidential, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, permanent position. The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits, including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. An annual vaccination against influenza is required. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499225 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. Screening will begin immediately, and the search will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. Priority will be given to applications received by 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on November 19, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 24 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 19 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
