    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499522/administrative-program-support-1-korey-stringer-institute": {
      "title": "Administrative Program Support 1 - Korey Stringer Institute",
      "description": "Administrative Program Support 1 - Korey Stringer Institute Apply now Search #: 499522 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Administrative Services JOB SUMMARY The Korey Stringer Institute (KSI), part of the Department of Kinesiology in the College of Agriculture, Health and Natural Resources, at the University of Connecticut, seeks applicants for a full-time Administrative Program Support 1. The Administrative Program Support 1 position supports the day-to-day operations of the Korey Stringer Institute (KSI), including supporting research studies, event planning, service projects, and advocacy work. The successful candidate will perform the routine administrative functions of the office; coordinate workflow and process administrative paperwork; provide financial support to KSI; are responsible for regular communications with university offices and outside agencies to request or provide information or to clarify procedures; and perform other duties as assigned. The successful candidate must have administrative skills and the desire to contribute to the business operations of KSI, as well as be open-minded, efficient, process-oriented, organized, and customer service driven. The position will report to the CEO of the Korey Stringer Institute and will be based on the Storrs Campus. About the Institute The Korey Stringer Institute’s mission is to provide research, education, advocacy, and consultation to maximize performance, optimize safety and prevent catastrophic injury for the athlete, warfighter, and laborer. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Serve as the main point of contact for the Korey Stringer Institute (KSI) at its Gampel Pavilion location. Facilitate inquiries from central offices. Provide administrative support to KSI Director and faculty. Maintain schedules for managers, supervisors, and other personnel. Schedule meetings, conferences, and day-to-day travel for the Institute; process paperwork and reimbursements. Assist the CEO of KSI with drafting and disseminating interdepartmental communications. Responsible for purchasing, including Pro-Card purchases, and maintaining all associated records. Responsible for MarketPlace order fulfillment for department entrepreneurial services. Communicate gift receipts to donors for the Department received through Foundation funding; process RFD and transfers through the Papersave system. Provide guidance and support to undergraduate student workers, including the hiring process and coordinating schedules. Assist with communications/marketing for the KSI and its programs. Responsible for facility maintenance needs and issues for the Gampel Pavilion location. Submit work orders and supervise the work and completion of repairs or maintenance needed. Handle, process, and coordinate requests to access labs for faculty, students, and staff. Other related duties as required. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Associate’s degree and two to three years of related experience or equivalent combination of education and experience. Demonstrated experience working in a highly demanding and fast-paced office environment. Demonstrated interpersonal skills and experience working with individuals of diverse backgrounds. Demonstrated verbal and written communication skills. Demonstrated organizational skills with attention to detail. Demonstrated customer service skills. Experience utilizing Microsoft Office applications. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in a related field, preferably in the medical/health field, and two years of related experience or equivalent combination of education and experience. Demonstrated experience using software, such as Concur and Huskybuy. Experience using Kuali Financial Systems, or similar. Experience with fiscal or bookkeeping functions in the daily operations of an office or organization. Accounts payable experience including reconciliations and use of basic accounting principles and arithmetic. Experience in a higher education/university setting. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $45,842 to $52,500. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves header at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA) and look for information specifically identified for UCPEA, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, one-year, end-dated position subject to renewal depending upon funding and performance. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499522 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 PM on October 30, 2026, with the review of applications beginning at that time. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 15 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499342/preaward-specialist-faculty-shared-services": {
      "title": "Pre-Award Specialist - Faculty Shared Services",
      "description": "Pre-Award Specialist - Faculty Shared Services Apply now Search #: 499342 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Grants and Contracts JOB SUMMARY The Office of the Vice President for Research (OVPR) is competitively recruiting talented grants and contracts/sponsored project professionals to join our research administration team. Sponsored Program Services (SPS) is responsible for administering a portfolio of $375M in annually awarded funding across all UConn campuses and UConn Health. We are a top-ranked public research university and land grant institution, rurally situated in the “Quiet Corner” of Northeast Connecticut. The Pre-Award Grants and Contracts Specialist provides day-to-day management and oversight for a high volume of pre-award administration. This position currently involves a hybrid work schedule with work to be conducted on site on occasion in Storrs, CT. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Serves as a liaison between investigators, academic units, and other administrative offices throughout the proposal preparation and review process. Provides technical assistance, guidance, and advice to faculty, administrators, and other professional staff for sponsored project administration. Reviews financial and administrative aspects of proposals or transactions to ensure compliance with federal and state statutes, University policy, and sponsor guidelines and requirements. Following University policies, sponsor requirements, and state and federal requirements, identifies and assists with resolving grant and contract issues pertaining to budget, cost sharing, fiscal, administrative, and procedural constraints, and other similar matters. Maintains records in accordance with University, state, federal, and sponsor requirements. Provides records as requested and collaborates with SPS leadership in response to audits. May participate in policy and procedure discussions and recommend policy or procedural changes as appropriate to improve efficiency and effectiveness. May participate in the development and delivery of sponsored program training. Performs related work as required. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in a related field and four years of related experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Demonstrated verbal and written communication and interpersonal skills. Demonstrated time management, follow-through, and organizational skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience with and knowledge of Uniform Guidance and/or the Federal Acquisition Regulations (FAR). Experience preparing and/or reviewing proposals within electronic research administration systems (such as grants.gov, research.gov, NSPIREs, and eRA Commons). Experience working in research administration at an institution of higher education. Experience working in a high volume, high production, and customer-facing professional environment. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $64,405 to $83,727. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves header at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA) and look for information specifically identified for UCPEA, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, permanent position. Candidates must be able to work on site on occasion in Storrs, CT. The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits, including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499342 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on November 6, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 15 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 06 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
