    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499886/visiting-assistant-professor-of-german": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor of German",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor of German Apply now Search #: 499886 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Faculty Temporary JOB SUMMARY The German Section of the Department of Literatures, Cultures & Languages at the University of Connecticut in Storrs is seeking to hire a Visiting Assistant Professor of German beginning in the Spring Semester 2027. The successful candidate will be fluent in German and English and will be expected to teach advanced courses in both languages. The position requires expertise in film, literary and cultural studies in the German-speaking world and demonstration of a strong interest in teaching a variety of German courses that are currently part of our curriculum, such as GERM 2400E The Environment in German Culture, GERM 1920 Cyborgs, Robots, and Androids in the German Imaginary, GERM 1169 Contemporary Germany in Europe, GERM 3251 German Culture Across Time, etc. For a full course listing, see our Undergraduate Catalog. The German Studies section at UConn is among the most vibrant and successful German programs in the country. Its faculty members have an outstanding research and publication record, and the program is home to many interdisciplinary programs and projects. Many of our students are dual degree majors in our signature EUROTECH (German and Engineering) and EUROBIZ (German and Business) programs. The successful candidate will find a welcoming community of scholars, teachers, graduate students, and undergraduates who work together to provide an innovative curriculum that prepares students for today’s world. Founded in 1881, UConn is a Land Grant and Sea Grant institution and member of the Space Grant Consortium. It is the state’s flagship institution of higher education and includes a main campus in Storrs, CT, four regional campuses throughout the state, and 13 Schools and Colleges, including a Law School in Hartford, and Medical and Dental Schools at the UConn Health campus in Farmington. The University has approximately 10,000 faculty and staff and 32,000 students, including nearly 24,000 undergraduates and over 8,000 graduate and professional students. UConn is a Carnegie Foundation R1 (highest research activity) institution, among the top 25 public universities in the nation. Through research, teaching, service, and outreach, UConn embraces diversity and cultivates leadership, integrity, and engaged citizenship in its students, faculty, staff, and alumni. UConn promotes the health and well-being of citizens by enhancing the social, economic, cultural, and natural environments of the state and beyond. The University serves as a beacon of academic and research excellence as well as a center for innovation and social service to communities. UConn is a leader in many scholarly, research, and innovation areas. Today, the path forward includes exciting opportunities and notable challenges. Record numbers of undergraduate applications and support for student success have enabled the University to become extraordinarily selective. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES We are looking for someone to teach courses in film, literary, and cultural studies in the German-speaking world, with a teaching load of seven courses per academic year. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Ph.D. in German or a related field by the time of appointment. Equivalent foreign degrees are acceptable. Native or near native fluency in German and English. Experience teaching at a college or university. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience teaching German Literature and Culture courses at a college or university. Experience in teaching both large lecture courses (such as German film taught in English) and small courses in a program that includes many dual degree students. Commitment to program building and advising student activities (German Club, Kaffeestunde, etc.). COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $60,000 to $65,000. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves and Engagement & Learning headers at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the American Association of University Professors (AAUP) bargaining unit and look for information specifically identified as AAUP, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, 9-month, non-tenure track position with an anticipated start date of January 1, 2027, annually renewable for up to three years. The successful candidate’s academic appointment will be at the Storrs campus. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the American Association of University Professors UConn Chapter (AAUP). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499886, and submit the following application materials: A cover letter , Curriculum vitae , Teaching statement (including teaching philosophy, teaching experience, commitment to effective learning, concepts for new course development, etc.); Commitment to diversity statement (including broadening participation, integrating multicultural experiences in instruction and research and pedagogical techniques to meet the needs of diverse learning styles, etc.); Sample journal articles or books Name and Contact information for 3 professional reference s. Evaluation of applicants will begin and continue until the position is filled, with preference given to applications received by October 31, 2026. For more information regarding the Department of Literatures, Cultures & Languages and its German Section, please visit the department website and the German at UConnGerman website. At the University of Connecticut, our commitment to excellence is complemented by our commitment to building a culturally diverse community. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on December 13, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, genetics, disability, age, or veteran status. The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO Employer. Advertised: Oct 14 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Dec 13 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499245/iacuc-specialist": {
      "title": "IACUC Specialist",
      "description": "IACUC Specialist Apply now Search #: 499245 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Research JOB SUMMARY UConn’s Research Integrity and Compliance Services within the Office of the Vice President for Research, is seeking an experienced Institutional Animal Care and Use Committee (IACUC) professional to join our team. Reporting to the Director of Research Compliance, the IACUC Program Specialist (Administrative Program Support 4) will work closely with researchers, IACUC program staff, Animal Care Services, and other University offices to ensure the University’s animal care and use program maintains compliance with federal, state, and local regulations and policies governing the use of vertebrate animals in research and teaching. This position does not involve the provision of direct care to animals but is a research compliance oversight position. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Performs administrative pre-review of protocol applications, facilitates veterinary and ancillary review processes, and provides review process oversight to ensure protocols are approved in a timely manner. Maintains internal database of animal protocols. Advises researchers on protocol submission development and matters related to regulations regarding the care and use of vertebrate animals in research and teaching. Assists with programmatic functions including protocol-grant congruency reviews, annual reporting (USDA, AAALAC, OLAW), memorandums of understanding with collaborating institutions, and other internal and external communications and reports. Coordinates and participates in semi-annual animal housing and use facility inspections. Compiles reports and performs follow-up processes as required. Promotes the University as a key player in the IACUC compliance areas by maintaining professional relationships with peers and regulatory representatives and participating in professional development activities to maintain current knowledge of regulations and national accreditation standards. Assists with the development and implementation of policies and guidelines, educational materials, presentations, and post-approval monitoring activities. Contributes to the writing of IACUC Office Standard Operating Procedures. Revises IACUC protocol forms and checklists as needed. Facilitates IACUC or other research compliance stakeholder meetings as needed, including logistical arrangements and preparation and distribution of decisions, agendas, minutes, etc. Participates in the planning and preparation for and execution of regulatory and accreditation visits and other IACUC related activities. Performs other related duties as assigned. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in biological sciences or related field and four to five (4 -5) years of related research administrative experience, or equivalent combination of education and experience. At least two of those years of administrative experience must be in an academic research compliance setting requiring knowledge and understanding of applicable regulations. Demonstrated experience with federal, state, and local regulations and policies pertaining to the care and use of animals used for research and teaching. Experience utilizing organizational skills to effectively multi-task to meet deadlines and troubleshoot problems. Experience exercising a wide range of independent judgement and discretion and maintaining confidentiality. Demonstrated interpersonal and communication skills (written and oral) and experience working with a highly diverse group of people, both independently and as part of a team. Demonstrated experience using Microsoft Office 365 suite. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience involving the use of animals in a research, medical, or similar institutional settings and a demonstrated understanding of scientific methodology. Certified Professional IACUC Administrator (CPIA) or eligible within one year of hire. Experience with electronic protocol management systems, including direct experience with implementation of an electronic system. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $64,405 to $83,727. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves header at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA) and look for information specifically identified for UCPEA, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, permanent position. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499245 to upload a resume , cover letter, and contact information for three (3) professional references . This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on November 3, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 13 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 03 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499842/visiting-assistant-extension-educator-4h-youth-development": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Extension Educator 4-H Youth Development",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Extension Educator 4-H Youth Development Apply now Search #: 499842 Work type: Full-time Location: New Haven County Extension Ctr Categories: Faculty Extension Educator JOB SUMMARY The Department of Extension, New Haven County, a part of the College of Agriculture, Health and Natural Resources, at the University of Connecticut, in collaboration with the Connecticut Agricultural Experiment Station (CAES) seeks applicants for a full-time Visiting Assistant Extension Educator, 11-month position. This person will focus on 4-H youth development specifically in the areas of food, agriculture and natural resources literacy in New Haven County. State and multi-state programming may be expected. Additionally, this position will plan, deliver, and evaluate school-based programs to increase youth STEM knowledge and skills. The Visiting Assistant Extension Educator will report to the Department of Extension Head and will be based in North Haven, Connecticut. The successful candidate shall expand an active 4-H youth development program with a focus on food, agriculture, and natural resources literacy. The successful candidate will provide leadership for the 4-H community club program in New Haven County, generate financial and in-kind resources to support 4-H programs, manage county-based 4-H volunteers, share responsibility with the Middlesex Educator, for conducting the annual Middlesex & New Haven 4-H County Fair, and actively contribute to the UConn 4-H Youth Development Team and its goals. Additionally, in collaboration with CAES, the successful candidate will plan, deliver, and evaluate school-based programs to increase youths’ STEM knowledge and skills, contributing to a better prepared scientific workforce. School-based programs may include school enrichment, in-school or after-school clubs, and special interest programs. About the Department The Department of Extension in the College of Agriculture, Health and Natural Resources works collaboratively with partners in all 169 municipalities across Connecticut, throughout the northeast region, and beyond. It is a non-tenure unit with 42 faculty and 33 programs and administrative staff. Additional grant-specific program personnel assist in solving problems and enhancing the wellbeing of our state population where they live, work, and learn. Faculty and staff conduct educational activities through eight-county/community-based centers and may be co-located with additional community/agency-based working partners. About the University Founded in 1881, UConn is a Land Grant and Sea Grant institution and member of the Space Grant Consortium. It is the state’s flagship institution of higher education and includes a main campus in Storrs, CT, four regional campuses throughout the state, and 13 Schools and Colleges, including a Law School in Hartford, and Medical and Dental Schools at the UConn Health campus in Farmington. The University has approximately 10,000 faculty and staff and 32,000 students, including nearly 24,000 undergraduates and over 8,000 graduate and professional students. UConn is a Carnegie Foundation R1 (highest research activity) institution, among the top 25 public universities in the nation. Through research, teaching, service, and outreach, UConn embraces diversity and cultivates leadership, integrity, and engaged citizenship in its students, faculty, staff, and alumni. UConn promotes the health and well-being of citizens by enhancing the social, economic, cultural, and natural environments of the state and beyond. The University serves as a beacon of academic and research excellence as well as a center for innovation and social service to communities. UConn is a leader in many scholarly, research, and innovation areas. Today, the path forward includes exciting opportunities and notable challenges. Record numbers of undergraduate applications and support for student success have enabled the University to become extraordinarily selective. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Develops, implements, and evaluates active extension programs on cutting-edge 4-H STEM related activities that foster state, regional and national recognition. Programming will be provided in support of 4-H community clubs, school enrichment, out-of-school programs, 4-H summer camps, 4-H volunteer development, and other areas as needed. Teaches youth and adult audiences in support of UConn 4-H and CAES. Works with UConn and CAES faculty, staff, scientists, and other partner organizations, in a multidisciplinary team environment to create and deliver age-appropriate program materials. Creates partnerships with other agencies and organizations, including schools, and actively seeks out grants and funding sources to support innovative community programs and outreach efforts. Creates scholarly materials appropriate for extension and CAES publications Develops, implements, and evaluates adult and youth volunteer programs including recruitment, training, management, evaluation, and recognition. Increase program visibility by effectively using available communication resources. Designs training opportunities and effectively communicate with adult volunteers and teens to help them assume leadership, management, education, and information delivery roles in support of the 4-H program. Other related duties as assigned. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree in nonformal or formal education, including agricultural and extension education; food, agricultural, environmental or health related sciences; youth development; or associated fields. Experience in educational program coordination and facilitation, that includes planning, organization, delivery, and evaluation. Knowledge of teaching methods and processes that are appropriate for youth and adult audiences. Demonstrated experience working cohesively with diverse audiences of youth, adults, and volunteers. Experience developing partnerships with other professionals and organizations to accomplish team goals. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS At least three years’ experience working with K-12 youth in the areas of education, food, agriculture, environment, or health. At least three years’ experience in managing or working with volunteers. Experience with integrated Extension programs and the land-grant university system. Demonstrated experience evaluating STEM programming and disseminating related scholarship through appropriate outlets, such as conferences and journals. Experience publishing peer-reviewed scholarships, Extension reports, or articles in electronic media that communicate program impacts and results. Experience in grantsmanship, particularly obtaining progressively larger grants and/or leading medium to large multi-disciplinary, multi-functional grant-funded projects. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $78,735 to $86,900. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves and Engagement & Learning headers at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the American Association of University Professors (AAUP) bargaining unit and look for information specifically identified as AAUP, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is an 11-month, full-time, temporary faculty position with an anticipated start date of November 13, 2026. It is a non-tenure track appointment that is anticipated to end November 12, 2027. Renewal of this appointment is based upon performance and the availability of funding. The successful candidate will work primarily at UConn’s New Haven County Extension Office located in North Haven, CT, with occasional travel to the Connecticut Agriculture Experiment Station located in New Haven, CT. Other related travel will be required including to the UConn Storrs Campus, other extension centers, and elsewhere in the state. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. The successful candidate will be required to have a valid driver’s license and reliable transportation for required travel, both in-state and out-of-state. The successful candidate may be required to work evening and weekend hours as required for the program. The successful incumbent must be willing and able to work occasional evening and weekend hours; must have reliable transportation and a valid driver's license; and must possess adequate physical strength, stamina, agility, and fitness to perform the required duties. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499842 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. For questions regarding this position, you may reach out to the search committee chair, Jen Cushman . This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on October 30, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499885/administrative-program-support-2": {
      "title": "Administrative Program Support 2",
      "description": "Administrative Program Support 2 Apply now Search #: 499885 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Administrative Services JOB SUMMARY Provides administrative support for Information Technology Services (ITS) Business Office operations. Serves as a resource for ITS staff, student employees, vendors, and university departments to support efficient, accurate, and compliant business operations. Administers and manages student labor for department, including the posting, processing and payroll for all ITS departments. Assists in compiling departmental financial activities to be used for budgetary monitoring and fiscal projections by ITS Business Office Manager. Reporting Structure Works under the general supervision of the ITS Business Office Manager and collaborates with ITS leadership, staff, student employees, vendors, Human Resources, Payroll, and university departments. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Administrative Responsibilities Supports ITS projects by monitoring financial activity, maintaining project records, and ensuring appropriate cost allocations. Compiles data and prepares reports used to monitor departmental expenditures, budgets, projects, and services. Processes purchase requisitions, purchase orders, and other procurement-related transactions. Reviews vendor invoices for accuracy and facilitates payment processing in accordance with University procedures. Serve as a resource for ITS staff, university departments, student employees, and vendors on administrative, procurement, payroll, and financial processes. Assists with tracking software agreements, subscriptions, maintenance renewals, and related documentation. Provides backup administrative support as needed, including coordinating and scheduling ITS Leadership meetings in collaboration with the administrative team. Performs related duties as required. Student Labor/HR Functions Coordinates student employee hiring, onboarding, and offboarding, including hiring documentation, employment transactions, system access requests, and records management. Supports student payroll administration by reviewing timesheets, monitoring deadlines, resolving discrepancies, and coordinating with Human Resources and Payroll as needed. Maintains student employment records and tracks funding allocations, work schedules, appointment dates, and earnings to support planning and compliance with university requirements. Guides supervisors and student employees on hiring procedures, payroll processing, employment policies, and administrative requirements. Monitors student employee appointments to ensure extensions, renewals, position changes, and terminations are processed timely. Maintains departmental records, files, and documentation in accordance with university policies and procedures. Maintains knowledge of university policies, procedures, financial systems, payroll requirements, and business office processes; provides guidance and outreach as appropriate. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree in business administration, accounting, finance, human resources, or a related field and at least two years of related professional experience. An equivalent combination of education and experience may be substituted for the degree and experience requirements. Experience performing administrative, financial, payroll, procurement, human resources, or business-office functions. Experience reviewing or reconciling financial or payroll transactions and researching or resolving discrepancies. Experience compiling, maintaining, and reviewing data, records, or reports. Experience using Microsoft Office applications, including Excel, Word, Outlook, and Teams, in a professional setting. Experience coordinating multiple administrative activities or processes with established deadlines. Experience preparing professional correspondence, reports, procedural instructions, or other administrative communications. Experience serving as a point of contact for employees, supervisors, vendors, customers, or organizational departments. Experience maintaining employee, payroll, financial, or other confidential records. Experience independently coordinating administrative processes involving multiple individuals, departments, or organizational units. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience supporting business or administrative operations in a higher education, public-sector, or similarly complex organization. Experience administering student employment processes, including hiring, onboarding, payroll review and finalization, appointment changes, and offboarding. Experience processing procurement transactions, reviewing invoices, and coordinating vendor payments. Experience monitoring budgets, reconciling financial activity, tracking expenditures, and preparing financial or operational reports. Experience with Core-CT, HuskyBuy, Kuali Financial Systems, or comparable enterprise financial, payroll, and procurement systems. Experience with Kuali Build or a comparable workflow and forms-management system. Advanced proficiency with Microsoft 365 applications, particularly Excel, Teams, Outlook, and SharePoint. Familiarity with basic accounting principles, cost allocations, and financial-reporting practices. Experience interpreting and communicating organizational policies, procedures, and administrative requirements. Demonstrated problem-solving skills and the ability to identify and resolve payroll, financial, procurement, or administrative discrepancies. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $53,943 to $70,126. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves header at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA) and look for information specifically identified for UCPEA, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499885 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on November 23, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 23 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 23 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
