    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499865/university-educational-assistant-3-uea3-executive-assistant-to-the-executive-leadership-team": {
      "title": "University Educational Assistant 3 (UEA3) - Executive Assistant to the Executive Leadership Team",
      "description": "University Educational Assistant 3 (UEA3) - Executive Assistant to the Executive Leadership Team Apply now Search #: 499865 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Administrative Services JOB SUMMARY Provides confidential executive, administrative, and operational support to the Vice President (VP) of Facility Services and University Planning (FSUP), as well as executive-level support to the Associate Vice President (AVP) of Facility Operations (FO), the Executive Director of University Planning, Design and Construction (UPDC), and other members of the FSUP executive leadership team, as assigned. This is a confidential exempt position, with dual emphasis on managing the schedule and activities of the VP of FSUP, as well as coordinating the day-to-day administrative activities under the direction of the VP of FSUP, while maintaining the highest level of confidentiality. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Serves as executive assistant and logistical point of contact for the Vice President (VP) of Facility Services and University Planning (FSUP). Coordinates a complex schedule of activities, coordinates meetings, travel arrangements, financial reimbursements, and logistics for the VP of FSUP, AVP of FO, and Executive Director of UPDC. Ensures that the VP and other executive leaders are fully prepared to participate in all scheduled meetings and activities. Maintains strict confidentiality while handling sensitive information, executive communications, and labor and administrative matters, regularly exercising discretion in the conduct of business and administrative activities. Handles a large volume of incoming communications and responds to inquiries from internal and external stakeholders on behalf of the VP of FSUP on routine matters and as directed. Conducts inquiries and research, reviews and summarizes information, drafts documents and professional correspondence for executive review. Schedules and coordinates recurring contractor business reviews and other departmental meetings, including preparing agendas, records and documents meeting minutes and notes, and tracks follow-up action items. Maintains complex day-to-day prioritization and management of the FSUP department calendars, monitors scheduling conflicts, and coordinates priorities across multiple areas. Assists in department initiatives, administrative processes, and special projects to support department and university goals. Plans and coordinates relevant logistics such as organizing agendas, scheduling and setting up meeting rooms, and managing catering for office-related events, meetings and departmental functions. Manages daily office operations by maintaining office supply inventory, distributes department mail, verifies department website information, and provides administrative support to ensure efficient workflow. Administer SharePoint file access permissions and coordinates software application and license requests and/or renewals to support departmental operations. Performs related duties as required. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Associate’s degree and three years of experience supporting the operations of an office, supporting management or leadership, or in a related administrative capacity. Education and training may be substituted for years of experience. Demonstrated analytical and interpersonal skills, with ability to negotiate and resolve problems of unusual difficulty. Experience providing executive-level administrative support and managing a complex schedule of executive activities or equivalent. Demonstrated ability to maintain strict confidentiality and to function effectively in ambiguous situations requiring the exercise of significant judgment and discretion. Demonstrated written and verbal communication skills. Experience with Microsoft Office Suite and its associated applications such as Outlook, Word, and excel, as well as PDF platforms and other scheduling tools. Demonstrated attention to detail in composing and formatting documents and spreadsheets. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree and one to two years of experience providing administrative support in a fast-paced business office within a large, complex organization. Two or more years of experience providing executive/administrative support in a higher education administrative office or similarly complex organization. Experience reviewing and improving administrative and internal operating procedures, performing analysis, interpreting and summarizing findings, and making appropriate recommendations; drafting correspondence, policies, reports, memoranda. Experience using Nitro Sign to administer electronic signature workflows for sensitive information and confidential business documents. Demonstrated knowledge of UConn administrative and fiscal policies and procedures. Experience using University enterprise systems, including Kuali Financial System (KFS), Core-CT, Concur, HuskyBuy, or similar enterprise applications. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $62,000 to $75,000. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves header at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is considered management/confidential and look for information specifically identified for management/confidential, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a 40 hour per week, full-time, 12-month permanent position. This position will work 8:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m., with a one-hour lunch, to provide coverage during the University's standard business hours. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. This position is categorized as Emergency Support Services/Essential Staff. Candidates must be willing and able to work during emergency closures/delayed openings due to inclement weather or for significant events that affect campus operations. Must have a willingness and ability to work evenings and weekends. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499865 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on November 30, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 23 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 30 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499843/assistant-associate-or-full-professor-quantum-science": {
      "title": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor, Quantum Science",
      "description": "Assistant, Associate or Full Professor, Quantum Science Apply now Search #: 499843 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Faculty Tenure Track JOB SUMMARY The Department of Mathematics and the Department of Statistics at the University of Connecticut (UConn) jointly invite applications for a full-time, 9-month tenured position at the rank of Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Professor in quantum science . This position is part of a multi-departmental cluster hire in quantum science—the first phase of a \"Quantum Futures Cluster\"— supporting UConn’s leadership in the NSF Quantum Technologies Engine in Connecticut (QuantumCT Engine). The hire is central to a major, long-term strategic investment to establish Connecticut as a national leader in quantum technology. To strengthen the research and educational missions identified in the strategic plans of the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences and the University, we seek a mathematician or statistician with expertise in quantum algorithms, quantum information science, optimization, and post-quantum cryptography to advance the goals of the QuantumCT Engine and create natural synergies with AI for ImpaCT, a university-wide initiative to drive AI innovations across Connecticut. We invite applications from candidates across a broad spectrum of quantum-related research in Mathematics or Statistics. The successful candidate will contribute to the development of next-generation quantum methodologies and help shape the future of mathematics and statistics in the quantum era. The QuantumCT Engine aims to advance American quantum innovation and secure the domestic quantum supply chain by accelerating the commercialization of quantum technologies for national defense, biotechnology and financial services. Through innovation, applied research leading to new technologies, support for inventors and entrepreneurs and workforce development, the QuantumCT Engine will advance quantum sensing, secure communications, computing, and materials through a shared testbed, deep-tech incubator, and translation pathways. Led by the Division of Academic Affairs and the Provost’s Office, the AI for ImpaCT initiative is focused on advancing artificial intelligence best practices across education, research, innovation, public engagement, and workforce development. UConn brings together expertise from across disciplines to help students, employers, communities, and policymakers understand both the opportunities and challenges presented by AI. The Department of Mathematics and the Department of Statistics at UConn are both highly active centers of research, education, and service with regional, national, and international prestige. The successful candidate will have a primary appointment in either department depending on their preference, with affiliation to the other, and will play a leadership role in UConn's growing quantum research ecosystem. Founded in 1881, UConn is a Land Grant and Sea Grant institution and member of the Space Grant Consortium. It is the state's flagship institution of higher education and includes a main campus in Storrs, CT, four regional campuses throughout the state, and 1 4 Schools and Colleges, including a Law School in Hartford, and Medical and Dental Schools at the UConn Health campus in Farmington. The University has roughly over 10,000 faculty and staff and 34,000 students, including nearly 26,000 undergraduates and over 8,000 graduate and professional students. UConn is a Carnegie Foundation R1 (highest research activity) institution, among the top 25 public universities in the nation. Through research, teaching, service, and outreach, UConn embraces diversity and cultivates leadership, integrity, and engaged citizenship in its students, faculty, staff, and alumni. UConn promotes the health and well-being of citizens by enhancing the social, economic, cultural, and natural environments of the state and beyond. The University serves as a beacon of academic and research excellence as well as a center for innovation and social service to communities. UConn is a leader in many scholarly, research, and innovation areas. Today, the path forward includes exciting opportunities and notable challenges. Record numbers of undergraduate applications and support for student success have enabled the University to become extraordinarily selective. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Conducting high-level, original research in the intersection of quantum science and mathematics/statistics. Seeking external funding. Supervising PhD students and mentoring postdoctoral scholars. Teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in mathematics or statistics and related quantum disciplines. Service to the departments, the university, and the broader professional mathematical and statistical community. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS A Ph.D. degree in mathematical sciences, statistics, or closely related disciplines. A distinguished record of academic accomplishment in one or more of the targeted areas for this position. A strong record of securing external research funding from federal agencies and/or industry partners. Ability to teach core courses in the appointed department(s) at both undergraduate and graduate levels. Demonstrated interpersonal and communication skills. Potential to contribute significantly to the QuantumCT project at UConn in building and sustaining a vibrant research program in quantum science. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Potential to interact productively with researchers working in the priority areas of the University of Connecticut and its College of Arts and Sciences such as artificial intelligence and other interdisciplinary fields. Demonstrated commitment to professional service and public engagement. COMPENSATION & BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $125,000 to $240,000. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves and Engagement & Learning headers at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the American Association of University Professors (AAUP) bargaining unit and look for information specifically identified as AAUP, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track position with an anticipated start date of August 23, 2027. The successful candidate’s academic appointment will be at the Storrs campus. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the American Association of University Professors UConn Chapter (AAUP). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499843 and submit the following application materials: A cover letter (candidates should clearly specify their target rank as either Assistant, Associate or Full Professor); Curriculum vitae; Research and Scholarship statement (innovative concepts that will form the basis of academic career, experience in proposal development, mentorship of graduate students, etc.); Teaching statement (including teaching philosophy, teaching experience, commitment to effective learning, concepts for new course development, etc.); Name and Contact information for 3 professional reference s. Review of applications will begin immediately. Full consideration will be given to applications completed and received before December 1, 2026. For more information, please visit the Department of Math and the Department of Statistics websites. Inquiries can be addressed to the Search Committee Co-Chairs, Vasileios Chousionis or Ming-Hui Chen. At the University of Connecticut, our commitment to excellence is complemented by our commitment to building a culturally diverse community. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on December 22, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 23 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Dec 22 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/498966/custodian": {
      "title": "Custodian",
      "description": "Custodian Apply now Search #: 498966 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Custodial Custodian Salary Range: $43,301.00-$54,108.00 Yearly Individuals new to state service start at the minimum of the pay plan. Link to Custodian Job Specification: https://www.jobapscloud.com/CT/specs/classspecdisplay.asp?ClassNumber=0429TC&R1=&R3= THIS POSITION IS OPEN TO CURRENT UCONN EMPLOYEES ONLY INTRODUCTION The State of Connecticut, University of Connecticut’s Student Union department has one Custodian job opening at the Storrs Campus. This is a permanent, full-time, 37.5 hours/week position. The starting hourly salary is $22.13/hour and is non-negotiable. Working under the supervision of the Lead Custodian, Supervising Custodian, or Building Services Manager, the successful candidate will be accountable for performing a full range of basic tasks in the cleaning and maintenance of the Student Union building. Below is the current shift and work schedule: 3rd shift, 11:00 PM – 7:00 AM, Saturday – Wednesday This position is categorized as Emergency Support Services/Essential Staff. The individual in this role must be willing to work during emergency closures/delayed openings due to inclement weather or for significant events that effect campus operations. Applicants must also be willing to respond to emergencies on overtime (nights, weekends, holidays). SELECTION PLAN In order to be considered for this job opening, you must meet the minimum qualifications as listed on the job opening and must specify your qualifications on your application. Applications will be evaluated to ensure that the Knowledge, Skill and Ability, Minimum Qualifications and Special Requirement sections of the position have been met. Ensure that your PageUp Application is complete and detailed before submitting it. You will not be able to make revisions once your application is submitted. Although it is not required, applicants are strongly encouraged to submit a cover letter, resume, and a list of three professional, work-related references along with their contact information. At any point of the recruitment process, applicants may be contacted via email and provided an opportunity to submit addition documentation which supports their qualification(s) for this position. These documents may include: a cover letter, resume, performance reviews, attendance records, supervisory references, licensure, etc., at the discretion of the hiring department. Applicants must meet the minimum qualifications and special requirements, as indicated, to apply for this position. If selected for an interview, you will be asked to provide the names, titles and phone numbers of three professional references. In addition, current State of Connecticut employee applicants at UConn or other State Agencies, may be asked to provide copies of their last two (2) performance appraisals and their CORE attendance records. Employment will be contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment physical examination, including drug testing, as well as a criminal background check. Please regularly check your email provided on your application for notifications. Please check your SPAM and/or Junk folders on a daily basis in the event an email provider auto-notification emails in a user's spam. PURPOSES OF JOB CLASS (NATURE OF WORK) Is accountable for performing the full range of basic tasks in the cleaning and maintenance of the Student Union building and other buildings under the responsibility of the Student Union and Event Services department. EXAMPLES OF DUTIES Performs custodial tasks and maintenance of such areas as administrative offices, meeting and function rooms, lounges, theatre, restrooms, lobby areas and outdoor areas in and around the Student Union building and other buildings under the responsibility of the Student Union. Dusts, mops, sweeps, scrubs, strips, waxes, and polishes floors using appropriate equipment, such as buffers, scrubbers and extractors. Washes, dusts, and polishes glass including windows, woodwork and walls, furniture and metal equipment. Collects and disposes of trash and performs recycling as instructed. Provides a report of equipment in need of repair, performs minor maintenance, run errands, inspects building for damage and reports conditions to a supervisor for action. May change light bulbs, lubricate door hinges, drawers or cabinets, etc. Remove snow and ice from stairways and walkways applying sand and salt as needed around the Student Union building. Move furniture and/or set-up meeting rooms for events. Performs other duties are required. KNOWLEDGE, SKILL, AND ABILITY Skills interpersonal skills; oral and written communication skills; Ability to follow oral and written instructions; operate, care for and perform minor maintenance on tools and equipment used in daily work; keep records. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Any experience and training which would provide the knowledge, skills and abilities listed above. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS A minimum of three years of custodial experience. Custodial experience in an educational setting. PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS Incumbent in this class must have adequate strength, stamina, physical agility and visual and auditory acuity, and must maintain such physical fitness as to be able to perform the duties of the class. A physical examination is required. WORKING CONDITIONS Incumbent in this class may be required to lift moderate to heavy weights and may be exposed to risk of injury from equipment and/or individuals. TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check and pre-employment physical. APPLICATION INSTRUCTIONS Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #498966. Although it is not required, applicants are strongly encouraged to submit a resume , cover letter , and a list of three professional, work-related references along with their contact information. This job posting is anticipated to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on November 6, 2026. CONCLUSION All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . Information concerning the University’s policies regarding the Cleary Act Statement, Non-Discrimination Policy, Accommodations for Applicants with Disabilities, and Recruiting Veterans can be found on UConn’s Job page. Please review the required notices and policy statements . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression. The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 23 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 06 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
