    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499854/applications-administrator-2": {
      "title": "Applications Administrator 2",
      "description": "Applications Administrator 2 Apply now Search #: 499854 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Information Technology JOB SUMMARY The University of Connecticut seeks a highly motivated and technically skilled professional to join Information Technology Services (ITS) as an Application Administrator 2. In this full-time role, you will provide advanced administration, support, and continuous improvement of enterprise applications supporting Facilities Services, including the AiM and ReADY platforms. You will serve as a key technical resource responsible for maintaining system reliability, enhancing business processes, and delivering technology solutions that support critical university operations. As an Application Administrator 2, you will support application configuration, troubleshooting, upgrades, integrations, reporting, and implementation activities. Working closely with functional users, technical teams, and vendors, you will analyze requirements, resolve complex issues, and recommend solutions that improve service delivery and operational efficiency. You will also develop and maintain Power BI reports and dashboards that transform data into actionable insights for Facilities Services leadership and stakeholders. Leveraging strong analytical and problem-solving skills, you will support system integrations, automation initiatives, and enterprise reporting solutions while helping ensure the security, availability, and performance of critical applications. This position offers an opportunity to work across diverse technologies and collaborate with stakeholders throughout the University to deliver innovative and reliable technology solutions. This position is designated as a hybrid role, requiring a minimum on-campus presence of three (3) days per week at the Storrs campus. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Provide advanced administration, configuration, and production support for enterprise applications and related integrations across multi-tiered application environments. Manage application configurations, user access, groups, roles, privileges, and other security-related settings in accordance with university policies and standards. Monitor application health, logs, integrations, data quality, and related technical dependencies; prioritize, troubleshoot, and resolve complex technical issues and service requests with minimal supervision; and develop processes that support application availability, reliability, and service continuity. Plan, coordinate, test, and support new application implementations, upgrades, migrations, integrations, enhancements, and other system changes from requirements through production deployment. Identify dependencies and risks and perform appropriate unit, integration, regression, and end-to-end testing. Work directly with application owners, functional stakeholders, vendors, and other technical teams to troubleshoot defects, resolve integration and operational issues, coordinate technical support requests, and support application development and enhancement activities. Identify manual, inefficient, or legacy processes and develop or implement appropriate technical improvements using scripting, APIs, automation frameworks, reusable components, or other technologies. Research, evaluate, prototype, recommend, and support implementation of technologies and technical approaches that improve application reliability, maintainability, operational efficiency, reporting capabilities, or user experience. Support, configure, test, troubleshoot, and enhance integrations between enterprise applications and related systems, including REST and SOAP web services, authenticated APIs, data interfaces, and associated technical dependencies. Write, analyze, and optimize SQL queries used for application support, troubleshooting, reporting, data validation, data extraction, transformation, integration, and operational analysis. Collaborate with functional and technical stakeholders to understand business processes; elicit, analyze, and document requirements; and translate business needs into maintainable solutions for applications, integrations, reports, dashboards, and system enhancements. Serve as a primary technical contributor for application upgrades, migrations, integrations, reporting implementations, and modernization initiatives. Communicate technical concepts, limitations, risks, alternatives, and project status clearly to technical and non-technical audiences. Develop and maintain functional, administrative, and technical documentation, including application configurations, implementation records, technical project summaries, integration specifications, reporting processes, automation routines, operational procedures, and troubleshooting guidance. Respond to inquiries from university departments and collaborate with application owners, business partners, vendors, and other ITS teams to resolve technical and operational issues and support cross-functional initiatives. Share technical knowledge, reusable solutions, and operational practices with team members; provide technical guidance and mentorship to less-experienced staff, student workers, or project participants as appropriate; and develop or facilitate demonstrations, knowledge-sharing sessions, and training for ITS colleagues and functional users. Represent the department at technical meetings, working groups, demonstrations, training sessions, and other university activities as appropriate. Support the confidentiality, integrity, and availability of University information as part of the University Information Security Program. Perform related duties as required. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Associate degree and six years of related experience, OR bachelor’s degree and four years of related experience, OR eight years of related experience; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience administering, supporting, and implementing enterprise applications in a production environment, including serving as a key technical contributor for application upgrades, migrations, implementations, integrations, or other significant technical initiatives. Demonstrated proficiency in writing SQL queries for relational database systems such as Oracle, Microsoft SQL Server, MySQL, or PostgreSQL. Experience supporting digital process automation (DPA) tools with complex workflows and multi-step business processes for example, Kuali Build, Microsoft Power Automate, Nintex, or similar platforms. Demonstrated ability to read, debug, and modify automation scripts in languages such as Python, PowerShell, Bash, or JavaScript and to make authenticated requests with REST or SOAP APIs and analyze JSON or XML responses. Demonstrated written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical audiences. Demonstrated understanding of information security, privacy, access control, and compliance practices within an enterprise environment. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively with technical staff, functional stakeholders, vendors, and management in a cross-functional environment. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience supporting applications in higher education or other complex operational environments including facilities management and planning design and construction. Experience remotely administering or troubleshooting systems using SSH, Remote Desktop, or equivalent tools. Experience designing and supporting Power BI solutions, semantic models, dashboards, paginated reports, and on-premises data gateways or equivalent reporting platforms. Experience applying AI-assisted development tools such as OpenAI Codex, Claude Code, GitHub Copilot to support application administration, automation, troubleshooting, and code creation, including agent-based workflows. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $84,880 to $110,344. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves header at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA) and look for information specifically identified for UCPEA, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499854 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on October 30, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 16 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Oct 30 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/en-us/job/499829/assistant-director-individualized-and-interdisciplinary-studies-program": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Individualized and Interdisciplinary Studies Program",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Individualized and Interdisciplinary Studies Program Apply now Search #: 499829 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Student Programs and Services JOB SUMMARY Reporting to the Director of the Individualized and Interdisciplinary Studies Program (IISP), the Assistant Director will develop and deliver program content for the Individualized Major (IMJR) Program, University Scholar Program, and several interdisciplinary minors. The core of the Assistant Director’s work will involve developing and coordinating program content and delivery; advising pre- and current individualized majors; collaborating with faculty and academic administrators; leading and coordinating committee meetings and projects; monitoring student progress toward degree completion; and coordinating a wide range of services and activities for students served by the office’s programs. The Assistant Director will be a highly experienced higher education professional, well-informed about the range of undergraduate courses and programs available at the University. The Assistant Director will also be an effective problem solver, accustomed to working independently, and capable of managing academically oriented administrative tasks. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Serves as the “second in command” for the Individualized and Interdisciplinary Studies Program (IISP). Develops, plans, and coordinates efforts towards establishing new programs, including leading various committees dedicated to developing structured major curriculum requirements and assessing program rigor. Serves as an instructor of the IMJR Gateway course for students interested in the Individualized Major Program; provides support to IISP Director on other IMJR-specific courses and curriculum. Administers the Individualized and Interdisciplinary Studies Program (IISP) application cycles throughout the academic year, including student outreach and recruitment and coordination of application and selection processes. Assists the Director in leading the expansion of IISP and IMJR programs on the regional campuses, assisting with developing strategic plans for addressing individual campus needs in collaboration with campus leadership and faculty. Advises students in developing individualized plans of study; may advise regarding alternative options for majors, complementary plans of study, and consistency with graduate school and career goals. Coordinates programs and events for IMJR students and collaborates with campus offices on joint programming efforts. Maintains appropriate files and records in order to compile and generate statistical reports related to program effectiveness and audit student records for IMJRs and IISP-administered minors to determine progress toward meeting academic requirements and to assess eligibility to graduate. Assists Director in planning and implementing scheduling and registration activities, orientation programs, and other activities, as assigned. Serves as a primary resource for students, faculty, parents, and others with questions about programs or academic policies; make referrals as appropriate. Assists in writing and/or editing informational and publicity materials for print, website, and social media platforms. Serves as communications liaison with IMJR Admissions Committee and faculty advisors, providing them with regular updates on student progress. Assists in the supervision of IISP student employees, interns, and/or peer advisors. Serves as a liaison with other university offices and external partners to provide enrichment opportunities – such as education abroad, internships, research, and professional development – for students served by IISP. Represents IISP and/or Enrichment Programs at UConn events, which may require occasional evening and weekend hours. Complete other duties, as assigned. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree in counseling, education, or relevant academic field AND four (4) years’ experience working with undergraduate students in a professional advising, counseling role, and/or teaching role. Two (2) years of experience must be serving as an advanced or lead team member. Demonstrated experience planning, coordinating, and implementing program services and activities. Demonstrated written and oral communication skills. Experience with interdisciplinary learning or research. Demonstrated organizational skills and demonstrated ability to manage multiple short- and long-term projects, including the proven ability to manage and perform administrative functions. Experience working with diverse, underrepresented, and/or first-generation students. Demonstrated ability to successfully advise undergraduate students and to interpret educational records and data related to student academic performance and progress. Experience compiling data and generating reports. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Doctoral degree. A degree in an interdisciplinary field. Professional work experience at a large university. Demonstrated experience prioritizing diversity, equity, and inclusion in practice. Experience teaching at the undergraduate level. Experience with supervision of student staff. Demonstrated ability to troubleshoot problems that interfere with students' academic progress and experience in working to resolve them effectively. Experience with assessment and program evaluation. Experience with database management. COMPENSATION AND BENEFITS The hiring range for this position is $76,000 to $83,000. An offer of employment, if made, will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s skill and experience, as determined by the University. For more information about benefits and other offerings available to University employees, we encourage you to review the Human Resources website and explore the sections under the Benefits & Leaves header at the top of the page. Under Benefits & Leaves, select Benefits to access an overview as well as additional information on topics such as paid time off, benefits, retirement, and other resources. As you explore these pages, please note that this position is covered by the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA) and look for information specifically identified for UCPEA, as provisions may vary by employee group. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, permanent position. The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits , including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499829 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . In your cover letter, please explain how you meet the minimum qualifications of the position as well as any preferred qualifications. Please note that the committee will not contact references until later in the search process, after discussion with applicants. Incomplete applications will NOT be considered. Applicants should include the search number in all correspondence. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on November 6, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Oct 16 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Nov 06 2026 Eastern Standard Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App"
